        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(release): preserve frozen validation compatibility",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFull release validation of a canonical frozen release target lost its trusted scenario-omission opt-in when release checks delegated package acceptance. Separately, a completed live-provider turn that crossed the terminal transcript deadline was not classified with the existing one-retry timeout policy.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Use the explicit `frozen_target_compatibility` mode throughout the trusted workflow chain, including package acceptance and Docker/Codex compatibility filtering, without exceeding GitHub's 25-input manual-dispatch limit.\n- Pass the release-checks opt-in into package acceptance.\n- Treat the exact `terminal timeout after <ms>` live-harness failure as retryable once, alongside existing transient test/provider timeouts.\n- Add focused contract tests for both paths.\n\n## User Impact\n\nFrozen release candidates can run bounded compatibility filtering through every release-validation child, while a one-off slow live-provider transcript receives one bounded retry. Deterministic failures still fail on the second attempt.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/package-acceptance-workflow.test.ts -- -t 'includes package acceptance in release checks'`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/ci-live-command-retry.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- Reproduced by Full Release Validation run 29437240793: package acceptance rejected the missing frozen-target opt-in, and OpenAI Terra crossed the 300000ms terminal deadline after Sol and Luna passed.\n",
